the [5-Chapter Combined Master Map](file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/gta%206%20mission%20workflow%20charts/flowchart_all_chapters_combined.png), each chapter column is framed with a distinct thematic color:\n- **Cyan (`#22d3ee`)**: **Chapter 1** — Leonida Keys & Key Lento\n- **Rose (`#f43f5e`)**: **Chapter 2** — Port Gellhorn & Kelly County\n- **Gold (`#fbbf24`)**: **Chapter 3** — Vice City Syndicate Expansion & Sinfrontera Heist\n- **Purple (`#a855f7`)**: **Chapter 4** — Ocean Beach & Airport Takedown\n- **Red (`#ef4444`)**: **Chapter 5** — The Climax, Compound Assault & Endings","thinking":"The color meanings seem to be defined in the flowchart rendering script and the markdown file. Background color is slate-gray. Investigating the yellow/cream color, it's used for the cards in the flowcharts. I will need to look deeper into the color definitions in the files.\n\n\nThe color code associations appear to be consistent across the markdown file and the rendering script. Investigating further, orange/peach represents major chapter climax missions while purple/lavender designates skippable side missions. Green badges highlight speedrun optimization, and pink heart cards signify relationship-based activities.\n\n\nWhite diamonds and rounded rectangles represent decisions, triggers, and communications within the game, with specific associations for each shape. White arrows indicate the main story flow, while colored arrows denote branches, warnings, and the speedrun route. Chapter column borders are assigned distinct colors.\n\n\n"}
