{"step_index":1086,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T22:48:06Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-25T17:48:06-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T17:48:06-05:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-25T17:48:06-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T17:48:06-05:00\nShowing lines 1-158 of 158\n1: Created At: 2026-11-24T20:37:39-05:00\r\n2: Completed At: 2026-11-24T20:37:39-05:00\r\n3: File Path: `file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK/output/SPEEDRUN_ROUTING_NOTES.md`\r\n4: Total Lines: 180\r\n5: Total Bytes: 12275\r\n6: Showing lines 1 to 150\r\n7: The following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\r\n8: 1: # Speedrun routing notes: build 1.0.2.1 (Xbox Series)\r\r\n9: 2: \r\r\n10: 3: ## Status\r\r\n11: 4: \r\r\n12: 5: **The mission progression graph has not been reconstructed.** No mission prerequisite, trigger, or protagonist\r\r\n13: 6: requirement was recovered. What was recovered is a verified mission inventory, a chapter grouping from two\r\r\n14: 7: independent sources, the progress-menu display order, four replay-entry links, and a small set of flow facts\r\r\n15: 8: read from a separately supplied folder of decompiled scripts.\r\r\n16: 9: \r\r\n17: 10: Do not route from these files as if they described unlock order. In `mission_order.json`, `null` means unknown.\r\r\n18: 11: \r\r\n19: 12: **Readable mission titles are not available.** Neither the dump nor the decompiled scripts contain display text.\r\r\n20: 13: The names in these files are the game's internal mission IDs.\r\r\n21: 14: \r\r\n22: 15: ## What was recovered\r\r\n23: 16: \r\r\n24: 17: | Finding | Source | Confidence |\r\r\n25: 18: |---|---|---|\r\r\n26: 19: | 145 mission table entries (ID, replay text key, grid texture) | `common.rpf` @ `0x219000`, XML root `CMissions` | Observed |\r\r\n27: 20: | 97 replay-menu entries under five chapter filters | `data.rpf` @ `0x12010000`, RBF0 root `uiProgressDataset`, category `missions_card` | Observed |\r\r\n28: 21: | Chapter grouping: 22 / 13 / 28 / 27 / 7 entries for chapte\n<truncated 8882 bytes>\nIL_LAW` is labelled `COA_SHIP`.\r\r\n139: 132: - **Main story versus side content:** not classifiable. ID prefixes such as `COM_`, `CTI_`, `CSC_`, `FT_`, `HO_`,\r\r\n140: 133:   `AO_`, and `UP_` are unexplained, so no Any% mandatory count is given.\r\r\n141: 134: - **Display titles:** unavailable. Only text keys were found (for example `PROG_INT_CHASE_DESC_REPLAY`); no\r\r\n142: 135:   localized text table was readable, and the decompiled scripts carry no string heap. Titles in\r\r\n143: 136:   `gta 6 mission workflow charts\\gta6_mission_flow_chart.md` and `GTAVI_MISSION_FLOW1.jpg` were checked against\r\r\n144: 137:   the dump: 3 of 145 candidate titles occur at all, and only as business or district names in location lists.\r\r\n145: 138: \r\r\n146: 139: ## Why the graph is not recoverable from this dump\r\r\n147: 140: \r\r\n148: 141: | Blocker | Measured fact |\r\r\n149: 142: |---|---|\r\r\n150: 143: | No executable | `game_scarlett_master.exe` is named in the manifests but absent, so there is no key material or native table |\r\r\n151: 144: | Encrypted name tables | Every RPF9 table of contents is high-entropy; extracted files have offsets, not names |\r\r\n152: 145: | Hashed script identifiers | All 3,010 script PSO files use 32-bit hashes for every struct and member name |\r\r\n153: 146: | Encrypted script strings | All 2,971 `LSNS` blocks are exact multiples of 16 bytes and repeat across files, the signature of a fixed-key block cipher |\r\r\n154: 147: | Opaque script data | 52.2 MB of `story000_script.rpf` (67%, 31 regions) is neither zlib nor plaintext |\r\r\n155: 148: | No mission anchor in scripts | Hashes of the mission IDs hit 1,263 times in `data.rpf` (control: 2) but only 12 times in th